{
  "meta": {
    "device": "Behringer FCB1010, stock firmware",
    "rig_note": "Marshall DSL201 removed 2026-09-14 (amp down, unknown how long/if it returns). Rig is Mesa Mark V:35 + Peavey Bandit 112 only. Prior 3-amp data (Marshall included) is recoverable from git history if Marshall comes back.",
    "mesa_control": "Voodoo Lab Control Switcher, set to PC mode (not CC). Each mesa_preset name below must be manually programmed onto Control Switcher itself (hold button 1 + button 4 while the switches are in the target combination) under the PC number listed in mesa_presets_pc, before sending this bank plan does anything useful.",
    "mesa_presets_pc": {
      "clean_eq_on": 1,
      "clean_eq_off": 2,
      "dirty_eq_on": 3,
      "dirty_eq_off": 4,
      "muted": 5
    },
    "mesa_preset_definitions": {
      "clean_eq_on": "Channel=Clean, Solo1=off, EQ=on",
      "dirty_eq_on": "Channel=Dirty, Solo1=off, EQ=on",
      "clean_eq_off": "Channel=Clean, Solo1=off, EQ=off (featured/solo clean tone)",
      "dirty_eq_off": "Channel=Dirty, Solo1=off, EQ=off",
      "muted": "Channel=Clean, Solo1=on (mute), EQ=on"
    },
    "mesa_control_switcher_midi_channel": 1,
    "switchtrack_midi_channel": 2,
    "switchtrack_pc_meanings_in_use": {
      "3": "Peavey audible (Switch-Track OUTB)",
      "7": "Mute (Peavey silent)"
    },
    "switchtrack_note": "Marshall's old OUTA leg is now unplugged/unused. Only PC3 and PC7 are meaningful with a single remaining Switch-Track amp.",
    "peavey_switching": "FCB1010 built-in relay SWITCH1 (fcb_switch1_relay: on=dirty, off=clean). Moved here from SWITCH2 on 2026-09-14, consolidating onto SWITCH1 since Marshall (SWITCH1's original amp) is out and not expected back. Polarity carried over from the SWITCH2 confirmation (2026-09-11) on the assumption that it's a property of Peavey's own footswitch jack, not of which FCB1010 relay drives it - NOT independently re-verified on SWITCH1 yet.",
    "mesa_modes_note": "Bank 0 = Clean-oriented section bank: Mesa Clean alone (both EQ states) + Mesa Clean x Peavey combos (both EQ states x both Peavey states), no Peavey-alone. Bank 1 = Dirty-oriented section bank, same shape with Mesa Dirty. Mixes single-amp and stereo-combo tones per bank for dynamics within a song section, rather than segregating by category. Bank 9 = single-amp reference for both amps (still has Peavey Clean/Dirty alone, if still wanted)."
  },
